 "notes": {
  "method": "Muristan block (Greek Orthodox market, 1900s): 2 storeys of honey-cream ashlar, ground-floor round-arched shopfronts with fanlights and teal/green steel doors or grey roll-downs, upper floor of round-arched windows and small balconies with black railings (notes 1.6, 1.7, 2.6; F01 from the Redeemer tower shows the blocks and their long red-tile hipped roofs). Edge 4 (NW face on the NE diagonal) is the far left of D05: shops under the big beige retractable awnings (shown as shed canopies at 3.4-4.1 m, 2.1 m deep), grey roll-downs. Edge 1 (south, on the east lane) meets the pink-pier arcade at its west end (D07, request).",
  "roof": "Real roof: red-tile hipped (F01, F03, D07, D08). Left flat here: build_city's hip roof uses the oriented bounding box and would overhang this footprint by metres (profile request). 'domes': 1 where set only keeps the vernacular lime-dome field (5-8 domes) off a roof that is really tiled."
 },
